{"id":"dtw_rbf_kernel","title":"Exponential transform of DTW","family":"kernel","definition":"reference","intro_en":"This construction first selects the minimum-cost DTW path and then exponentially transforms its squared distance. The animation shows the path calculation before the score conversion. Although the formula resembles a Gaussian kernel, replacing Euclidean distance by DTW does not automatically preserve positive semidefiniteness.","intro_zh":"该构造先选择最低代价 DTW 路径，再对距离平方做指数变换。动图先展示路径计算，再展示分数转换。将欧氏距离替换成 DTW 不自动保留高斯核的半正定性。","steps_en":["Build squared local costs and a monotone DTW recurrence.","Select the path with the least accumulated discrepancy.","Use that accumulated cost as DTW squared in exp(-gamma*cost).","Interpret the decreasing score with gamma=0.7 and the stated local norm."],"steps_zh":["构造平方局部代价与单调 DTW 递推。","选择累计差异最小的路径。","把该累计代价作为 DTW 平方代入 exp(-gamma*cost)。","结合 gamma=0.7 和明确的局部范数理解该递减分数。"],"formula":"K=exp(-0.7*DTW(x,y)^2), DTW uses squared costs then square root","caveats_en":["A DTW-based exponential may produce an indefinite Gram matrix. Do not infer kernel-method guarantees from its name.","The value changes with the path band, local cost and distance normalization."],"caveats_zh":["DTW 指数形式可能得到不定 Gram 矩阵；不能从名称推断核方法保证。","路径窗口、局部代价和距离归一化都会改变结果。"],"sources":[{"label":"tslearn: DTW definitions and path constraints","url":"https://tslearn.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user_guide/dtw.html"},{"label":"Cuturi (2011): local-kernel conditions for global alignment","url":"https://marcocuturi.net/Papers/cuturi11fast.pdf"}],"x":[0.2,0.4,1.1,2.4,3.2,2.5,1.2,0.3,-0.4,-0.1],"y":[0.1,0.3,0.5,1.2,2.6,3.1,2.3,1.1,0.2,-0.3],"input_label":"Deterministic illustrative arrays; no benchmark data","parameters":{"gamma":0.7,"base_distance":0.4472135954999581,"squared_distance":0.20000000000000015},"result":{"label":"kernel score","value":0.8693582353988057,"detail":"The explicit definition and parameters shown on this card."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Compare sampl